ACLaniakea: stop duplicate proc_mkdir() WARNs from the ported OPlus modules.

Applies to the mport tree (the sweep_oplus_modules.sh mirror).  Needs
kernel-compat/include/oplus_proc_compat.h copied to the mport root.
Modules built from kernel-compat/ (gloom, osvelte, proactive_compact,
memory_policy) carry the same change directly in the repo.

Every module below proc_mkdir()'d /proc/oplus_mem or /proc/task_info on its
own; each duplicate hit WARN() in proc_register and tainted the kernel.
The existing "dir/<node>" fallback already handles a NULL return, so the
fix only probes for the directory first.  oplus_ipc reuses d_oplus_binder.

--- a/mm/dump_tasks_mem/tasks_memory.c
+++ b/mm/dump_tasks_mem/tasks_memory.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <linux/uaccess.h>
 #include <linux/mm.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
+#include "oplus_proc_compat.h"
 
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_QCOM_KGSL)
 extern u64 kgsl_get_stats(pid_t pid);
@@ -214,7 +215,7 @@
 {
 	struct proc_dir_entry *root_dir_entry, *pentry;
 
-	root_dir_entry = proc_mkdir("oplus_mem", NULL);
+	root_dir_entry = oplus_proc_mkdir_shared("oplus_mem");
 	pentry = proc_create((root_dir_entry ?
 				"memory_monitor" : "oplus_mem/memory_monitor"),
 			S_IRUGO|S_IWUGO, root_dir_entry, &memory_monitor_fops);
